// Development workspace. The go.mod pins the declarative-agents modules at an
// upstream commit; this workspace points the build at the sibling checkout
// instead, so a change made there is visible here without re-pinning. Build
// with GOWORK=off to see what the pin alone resolves — that is what CI and a
// clone without the sibling checkout get.
//
// The sibling layout is this repository's documented convention (demo.yaml),
// and gh-* worktrees sit in the same parent directory, so these relative paths
// hold from a worktree as well.

go 1.26.3

use (
	.
	../declarative-agents/agent-core
	../declarative-agents/applications/catalog
)

// agent-core and applications/catalog each replace the magefiles module with a
// path relative to themselves. Both resolve to the same directory, but Go 1.26
// compares workspace replacements before resolving them and rejects the pair.
// A workspace-level replacement overrides both and names that directory once.
// The magefiles checkout is reached through this replacement rather than a use
// line: Go refuses to replace a workspace module at all versions.
replace github.com/mesh-intelligence/declarative-agents/magefiles => ../declarative-agents/magefiles
